# Files the running theme never reads: the chapter sources and the script
# that builds them, the Greek text the build quotes from, the keyword
# research, and the repository's own housekeeping. `git archive` leaves
# them out of a release zip (so does GitHub's "Download ZIP"):
#
#   git archive --format=zip --prefix=paulus/ -o paulus-$(sed -n 's/^Version:\s*//p' style.css).zip HEAD
#
# The installed theme keeps content/articles (the JSON texts the installer reads),
# assets/docs (the Martin notes are served to visitors), README.md and
# UPGRADING.md (the owner reads them on the site).
build.py        export-ignore
content/src/    export-ignore
sblgnt/         export-ignore
docs/           export-ignore
CHANGELOG.md    export-ignore
.gitignore      export-ignore
.gitattributes  export-ignore
